# Normalise all text files to LF in the working tree on every platform.
# Prevents CRLF churn when the repo is checked out / edited on Windows and
# then moved to macOS/Linux (which happened during the Win -> macOS move:
# 83 files showed up "modified" with nothing but CRLF -> LF changes).
#
# `text=auto`  -> Git auto-detects text vs binary
# `eol=lf`     -> text files always get LF in the working tree
#
# Applies retroactively after `git add --renormalize .` is run once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch line endings (belt-and-suspenders on top of
# text=auto's auto-detection).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
